WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.949 --> 00:00:03.670
Research is a glimpse of the future.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:09.849
Computer algorithms are capable of making
digital creatures walk, paint in the style

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:21.510
of famous artists, create photorealistic images
of virtual objects, simulate the motion of

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.570
fluids and a ton of other super exciting works.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:31.570
However, scientific papers are meant to communicate
ideas between experts. They involve lots of

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:36.730
mathematics and terminology. In Two Minute
Papers, I try to explain these incredible

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:42.530
scientific works in a language that is not
only understandable, but enjoyable, two minutes

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.690
at a time.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.370
Papers are for experts, but Two Minute Papers
is for you.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:51.940
If you're interested, let's celebrate science
together, there are two new science videos

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.910
coming every week, give it a shot, you'll
love it!

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:59.180
Thanks for watching and I am looking forward
to greeting you in our growing club of Fellow

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.220
Scholars!

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:00.880
Cheers!

